And Jesus says, don't store up for yourself treasures on earth because it's not going to lead to the satisfaction that you think it is.

213
00:18:08,780 --> 00:18:15,780
Jesus is pointing out something we all know deep down but rarely allowed to influence our decisions.

214
00:18:15,780 --> 00:18:17,780
Earthly wealth is fleeting.

215
00:18:17,780 --> 00:18:24,780
Every effort to store up stuff on earth will not accomplish what we want it to accomplish in our hearts and our lives.

216
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:31,780
So Jesus' solution is sell everything, live in the plains.

217
00:18:31,780 --> 00:18:32,780
No.

218
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:34,780
It's not that crazy.

219
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:43,780
He just says, store up your stuff, store up different kind of stuff in a more reliable location.

220
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:47,780
Firstly, he says, store up your stuff in heaven.

221
00:18:47,780 --> 00:18:52,780
Now, this is broadly misinterpreted, right?

222
00:18:52,780 --> 00:18:56,780
We think of heaven mostly influenced more by culture than by the Scriptures.

223
00:18:56,780 --> 00:19:01,780
We think of heaven as this, like, spiritual realm in the sky that we're going to go to when we die.

224
00:19:01,780 --> 00:19:07,780
And storing up treasures in heaven means that if we do good things on earth, then we'll have a bigger mansion in heaven.

225
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:10,780
That's not actually what Jesus is saying here.

226
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:16,780
Heaven, in the Hebrew mind, was actually the place where God's presence dwelled with God's people.

227
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:21,780
So heaven for Jesus is the kingdom of God.

228
00:19:21,780 --> 00:19:24,780
Investing in the kingdom of God on earth as it is in heaven.

229
00:19:24,780 --> 00:19:29,780
It's doing kingdom things here and now because heaven will come to earth.

230
00:19:29,780 --> 00:19:36,780
And what we do with the kingdom in mind on earth will last as the kingdom comes to earth.

231
00:19:36,780 --> 00:19:40,780
So he says, invest in heavenly things.

232
00:19:40,780 --> 00:19:49,780
And the treasures he's talking about here is that how we invest our possessions in a way that demonstrates our love for God and neighbor.

233
00:19:49,780 --> 00:20:04,780
If we use our stuff, our time, our energy, our resources, our wealth, if we invest these things in loving God with our whole heart, soul, mind, and strength, and loving our neighbor as ourselves, we will be storing up for ourselves treasures in heaven.

234
00:20:04,780 --> 00:20:10,780
We store up treasures for heaven when we use our stuff to do heavenly things on earth.

235
00:20:10,780 --> 00:20:16,780
My cliff notes summary of what Jesus is saying here is he says, I know, I know that you think.

236
00:20:16,780 --> 00:20:23,780
And this is, when I made my notes, I really thought this was bold that I was going to try and make a cliff notes version of what Jesus had to say.

237
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:25,780
Right?

238
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:25,780
Like this, it feels weird.

239
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:27,780
So take it for what it is.

240
00:20:27,780 --> 00:20:30,780
Ryan Miller's cliff notes version of Jesus.

241
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:31,780
Okay.

242
00:20:31,780 --> 00:20:37,780
I know you think accumulating stuff on earth will lead to security and pleasure.

243
00:20:37,780 --> 00:20:40,780
But in the end, it will lead to fear and greed.

244
00:20:40,780 --> 00:20:47,780
However, if you invest your stuff in my kingdom, it will give you the ultimate security and pleasure that you are seeking.

245
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:54,780
He goes on in verse 21, just for good measure, to make sure that we don't over-spiritualize this teaching or apply it to other people.

246
00:20:54,780 --> 00:20:55,780
Don't we tend to do that?

247
00:20:55,780 --> 00:20:56,780
Like, yeah, that's actually right.

248
00:20:56,780 --> 00:20:59,780
And that person needs to hear it because they have more money than I do.

249
00:20:59,780 --> 00:21:00,780
Right?

250
00:21:00,780 --> 00:21:03,780
So he makes just a really clear statement.

251
00:21:03,780 --> 00:21:07,780
Where your treasure is, there your heart will be also.

252
00:21:07,780 --> 00:21:18,780
So he says, if you're not sure if you're doing these things, if you're not sure if you're investing in, if you're storing up for yourself treasures in heaven, just look at how you spend your money.

253
00:21:18,780 --> 00:21:20,780
Look at what you treasure.

254
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:24,780
Look at the investment you put into things and stuff and money.

255
00:21:24,780 --> 00:21:28,780
Is it for my kingdom and my purposes?

256
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:31,780
Or your kingdom and your purposes?

257
00:21:31,780 --> 00:21:34,780
That will reveal to you where your heart is.

258
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:37,780
And again, remember, this isn't about guilt, condemnation, or shame.

259
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:40,780
And if you're feeling like, oh man, I've never really interacted with these teachings.

260
00:21:40,780 --> 00:21:44,780
I think I spend a lot of my time, money, and possessions on me.

261
00:21:44,780 --> 00:21:46,780
And I don't really think about the kingdom of God.

262
00:21:46,780 --> 00:21:48,780
Jesus isn't here trying to make you feel like a terrible person.

263
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:54,780
He's actually inviting you into the thing that's going to give you the life and experience that you're longing for.

264
00:21:54,780 --> 00:21:55,780
Amen.

265
00:21:55,780 --> 00:22:00,780
This is the creator of the universe saying, this is what you were intended to live for.

266
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:03,780
You're trying to get it in all the wrong places.

267
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:05,780
Searching for love?

268
00:22:05,780 --> 00:22:06,780
All the wrong places?

269
00:22:06,780 --> 00:22:13,780
This is Jesus' first teaching on money and wealth.

270
00:22:13,780 --> 00:22:15,780
Anybody uncomfortable yet?

271
00:22:15,780 --> 00:22:18,780
Okay, you guys are doing better than I am.

272
00:22:18,780 --> 00:22:19,780
All right.

273
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:20,780
Verse 22.

274
00:22:20,780 --> 00:22:23,780
The eye is the lamp of the body.

275
00:22:23,780 --> 00:22:28,780
So if your eye is healthy, your whole body will be full of light.

276
00:22:28,780 --> 00:22:33,780
But if your eye is bad, your whole body will be full of darkness.

277
00:22:33,780 --> 00:22:39,780
If then the light in you is darkness, how great is the darkness.

278
00:22:39,780 --> 00:22:46,780
Now you guys know exactly what Jesus is saying here, so I don't need any further explanation, right?

279
00:22:46,780 --> 00:22:50,780
This passage, it seems a bit cryptic.

280
00:22:50,780 --> 00:22:52,780
It seems a bit confusing.

281
00:22:52,780 --> 00:22:58,780
It seems like, Jesus, are you trying to hide some kind of deep spiritual truth in here that we don't know?

282
00:22:58,780 --> 00:22:59,780
No, you're just not Hebrew.

283
00:22:59,780 --> 00:23:01,780
So it doesn't make as much sense to you.

284
00:23:01,780 --> 00:23:05,780
But the passage would make a lot more sense to the original audience.

285
00:23:05,780 --> 00:23:13,780
It's a word play rich with Hebraic symbolism that I don't have the time, nor am I particularly qualified to explain to you.

286
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:22,780
I will be sharing a podcast in the newsletter this week that does an incredible job at deep diving just these two verses.

287
00:23:22,780 --> 00:23:31,780
So if you want to go deeper, if you want to go further, I will send that to you, and I hope that you find help in it.

288
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:35,780
But, I can't just skip it, so I'm going to do my best.

289
00:23:35,780 --> 00:23:39,780
Here's my best at simplifying what Jesus was saying.

290
00:23:39,780 --> 00:23:43,780
Hebrew culture, they viewed the eye as the window into the soul.

291
00:23:43,780 --> 00:23:47,780
It's not totally foreign from us, right?

292
00:23:47,780 --> 00:23:53,780
Like, when we have deep relationships with people, we look them in the eye, and we feel like there's this connection, this understanding.

293
00:23:53,780 --> 00:23:57,780
Like, I can understand who this person is better when I look them in the eye.

294
00:23:57,780 --> 00:23:58,780
In the eye, it's weird.

295
00:23:58,780 --> 00:24:01,780
Isn't it weird when you're talking to somebody and they won't look in the eye?

296
00:24:01,780 --> 00:24:04,780
It's like something shady, sketchy, something's going on here.

297
00:24:04,780 --> 00:24:10,780
So, the Hebrews, they had this idea that when you look somebody in the eye, it was a window through their, a window into their soul.

298
00:24:10,780 --> 00:24:20,780
And therefore, what they directed their attention to, where their eyes were gazing, where they were looking, where they were pursuing things, was ultimately revealing what was true about them on the inside.

299
00:24:20,780 --> 00:24:22,780
Does that make sense?

300
00:24:22,780 --> 00:24:28,780
Jesus makes a different version of this statement where he says, "Out of the overflow of the heart, the mouth speaks."

301
00:24:28,780 --> 00:24:29,780
Right?

302
00:24:29,780 --> 00:24:33,780
It's not what goes into the mouth that defiles the person, it's what comes out.

303
00:24:33,780 --> 00:24:40,780
This is the same idea, that where we direct, that you can tell a lot about a person's soul by how they direct their eyes.

304
00:24:40,780 --> 00:24:47,780
And it actually had become like a really, a word play here in Hebrew.

305
00:24:47,780 --> 00:24:53,780
Actually, in the Old Testament, the term good eye was regularly used to describe a generous person.

306
00:24:53,780 --> 00:25:02,780
If you had a good eye, people said, "Okay, there's something, you have peace internally with God and others, and that impacts the way that you handle your stuff."

307
00:25:02,780 --> 00:25:09,780
And bad eye was used to describe a stingy or selfish person.

308
00:25:09,780 --> 00:25:17,780
It's like when you see somebody being stingy or selfish or hoarding things for themselves, it reveals to you something about their internal relationship with God and others.

309
00:25:17,780 --> 00:25:20,780
And this is not a foreign idea.

310
00:25:20,780 --> 00:25:24,780
It's spoken in a foreign way, but I think we can all resonate with this, right?

311
00:25:24,780 --> 00:25:32,780
When you see somebody that's generous, that's kind, that's giving, you're like, "Oh, that person has something inside that's different."

312
00:25:32,780 --> 00:25:37,780
It reveals their relationship with God and neighbor.

313
00:25:37,780 --> 00:25:47,780
And Jesus is ultimately saying here that how you view and relate to God will determine whether you have a good eye or a bad eye, whether you live generously or selfishly, right?

314
00:25:47,780 --> 00:25:51,780
It's not just, we can't just change our behavior when it comes to generosity.

315
00:25:51,780 --> 00:25:55,780
You can't just say, "Oh, I heard a sermon on generosity, so I'm going to give more."

316
00:25:55,780 --> 00:25:57,780
It starts at the heart.

317
00:25:57,780 --> 00:26:02,780
It starts at how we view God and how we view others.

318
00:26:02,780 --> 00:26:10,780
John Mark Comer, who is one of the builders of this curriculum, summarizes this way.

319
00:26:10,780 --> 00:26:18,780
He says that, "Those with a good eye have an abundance mindset, and those with a bad eye have a scarcity mindset."

320
00:26:18,780 --> 00:26:23,780
So the abundant mindset says, "There is a good and loving creator.

321
00:26:23,780 --> 00:26:25,780
I am his beloved child.

322
00:26:25,780 --> 00:26:31,780
Everything that I have is a gift from him to be used and shared for his glory and the good of others."

323
00:26:31,780 --> 00:26:32,780
Right?

324
00:26:32,780 --> 00:26:38,780
There is a good heavenly father who created all of the earth and has given us all that we need for life and flourishing.

325
00:26:38,780 --> 00:26:39,780
He is good.

326
00:26:39,780 --> 00:26:41,780
He has a good purpose in mind.

327
00:26:41,780 --> 00:26:46,780
And if he is God, and if he is good, then there is more than enough resources.

328
00:26:46,780 --> 00:26:49,780
I don't need to be fearful or greedy.

329
00:26:49,780 --> 00:26:54,780
I don't need to fight and war and compete for stuff.

330
00:26:54,780 --> 00:26:56,780
I can live with an open hand.

331
00:26:56,780 --> 00:26:59,780
I can share what I have with those who are in need.

332
00:26:59,780 --> 00:27:03,780
Jesus will later go on to say in the Sermon on the Mount, "Look at the birds of the air.

333
00:27:03,780 --> 00:27:05,780
Look at the lilies of the field."

334
00:27:05,780 --> 00:27:09,780
They do not worry about what they are going to eat or what they are going to wear.

335
00:27:09,780 --> 00:27:17,780
Because they understand they are part of a bigger creation from a loving father who will provide.

336
00:27:17,780 --> 00:27:26,780
If this is how we view God, it will change everything about how we view our resources.

337
00:27:26,780 --> 00:27:29,780
It will lead us to a life full of peace and generosity.

338
00:27:29,780 --> 00:27:34,780
Or as Jesus puts it, we will have a good eye.

339
00:27:34,780 --> 00:27:39,780
The scarcity mindset says there is no benevolent God.

340
00:27:39,780 --> 00:27:46,780
He either doesn't exist or he isn't good, or at least he doesn't care about you and your family.

341
00:27:46,780 --> 00:27:49,780
This is a dog-eat-dog world, so I have to look out for myself.

342
00:27:49,780 --> 00:27:53,780
Other people are a competition for possible resources.

343
00:27:53,780 --> 00:27:57,780
And they ultimately get in the way of my security and my happiness.

344
00:27:57,780 --> 00:28:06,780
If this is how we view God, or a lack thereof, it will lead us to be consumed by fear and greed.

345
00:28:06,780 --> 00:28:09,780
Or as Jesus puts it, we'll have a bad eye.

346
00:28:09,780 --> 00:28:10,780
Right?

347
00:28:10,780 --> 00:28:19,780
We'll be consumed by just trying to carve out a path for ourselves where we feel secure and we feel happy.

348
00:28:19,780 --> 00:28:24,780
And it's like grasping at the wind.

349
00:28:24,780 --> 00:28:31,780
So, the reality is, I would guess, pastorally, as I've interacted with many of you in this room,

350
00:28:31,780 --> 00:28:36,780
the reality is that we probably all fall somewhere in between these two extremes.

351
00:28:36,780 --> 00:28:37,780
Right?

352
00:28:37,780 --> 00:28:41,780
Like, I painted the picture of as far on the opposite end of the spectrum as possible.

353
00:28:41,780 --> 00:28:45,780
I doubt that many of us would raise our hand and say,

354
00:28:45,780 --> 00:28:48,780
every moment of every day, I live with an abundance mindset.

355
00:28:48,780 --> 00:28:51,780
I know that God's going to provide for me.

356
00:28:51,780 --> 00:28:52,780
Everything I have is his.

357
00:28:52,780 --> 00:28:53,780
I freely give.

358
00:28:53,780 --> 00:28:54,780
I freely receive.

359
00:28:54,780 --> 00:28:55,780
Right?

360
00:28:55,780 --> 00:28:58,780
Like, that's, you know, Jesus.

361
00:28:58,780 --> 00:29:03,780
So, you know, somewhere on this scale, most of us are somewhere in the middle.

362
00:29:03,780 --> 00:29:07,780
Some of us might trend towards a scarcity mindset.

363
00:29:07,780 --> 00:29:14,780
But my goal here is for us to just think about where, how is it that I view God in light of the stuff that I have

364
00:29:14,780 --> 00:29:16,780
and the stuff that I feel that I need.

365
00:29:16,780 --> 00:29:24,780
And as your pastor, I really would love to stand up here and tell you that I embody the abundance mindset.

366
00:29:24,780 --> 00:29:32,780
I just, everything comes from God and I need nothing and I will go in peace.

367
00:29:35,780 --> 00:29:36,780
Right.

368
00:29:36,780 --> 00:29:37,780
So, here's the thing.

369
00:29:37,780 --> 00:29:39,780
I agree with these principles.

370
00:29:39,780 --> 00:29:40,780
Right?

371
00:29:40,780 --> 00:29:44,780
I listen to Jesus' teaching and I say, that is right and good, yes and amen.

372
00:29:44,780 --> 00:29:51,780
But then I wake up and I walk around my house and make note of the things that are broken

373
00:29:51,780 --> 00:29:53,780
and the things that need to be fixed.

374
00:29:53,780 --> 00:29:58,780
And I look at my wife and I look at my baby and I say, there's not going to be enough.

375
00:29:59,780 --> 00:30:00,780
There's never going to be enough.

376
00:30:00,780 --> 00:30:02,780
I've got to get a second Job.

377
00:30:02,780 --> 00:30:03,780
I've got to work harder.

378
00:30:03,780 --> 00:30:05,780
I've got to go do more stuff.

379
00:30:05,780 --> 00:30:11,780
And then I look at my friends who have more stuff than me and I'm like, man, why do they have more stuff than me?

380
00:30:12,780 --> 00:30:16,780
I'm slaving it out for the Lord and they have more stuff than me.

381
00:30:16,780 --> 00:30:22,780
Right?

382
00:30:22,780 --> 00:30:23,780
It's dark.

383
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:30,780
It's dirty and I feel myself being pulled towards it on a regular basis.

384
00:30:31,780 --> 00:30:38,780
And Jesus is saying, you think that having, like Ryan, you think that just a few more dollars in your savings account,

385
00:30:38,780 --> 00:30:44,780
one more appliance that's not broke, like you think that's actually going to make you happy and secure and satisfied.

386
00:30:44,780 --> 00:30:48,780
The next appliance will break next week.

387
00:30:48,780 --> 00:30:50,780
Like there's never going to be a season.

388
00:30:50,780 --> 00:30:55,780
I think many of us, we long for the season where we sit down on our couch and look around at everything.

389
00:30:56,780 --> 00:30:59,780
And nothing is broken and everything works.

390
00:30:59,780 --> 00:31:02,780
The engine light is not going to come on next week.

391
00:31:02,780 --> 00:31:05,780
And Jesus is saying, Jesus is saying that isn't reality.

392
00:31:05,780 --> 00:31:07,780
We live in a fallen world.

393
00:31:07,780 --> 00:31:08,780
Stuff breaks.

394
00:31:08,780 --> 00:31:10,780
Things get destroyed.

395
00:31:10,780 --> 00:31:12,780
Moth and rust, they eat.

396
00:31:12,780 --> 00:31:19,780
There's never going to be a season in your life where you feel like you have everything that you want.

397
00:31:19,780 --> 00:31:22,780
I mean, there's studies about wealthy people.

398
00:31:23,780 --> 00:31:27,780
I heard a story one time about a financial broker who was talking to a person with a million dollars.

399
00:31:27,780 --> 00:31:29,780
It was like, how much will be enough?

400
00:31:29,780 --> 00:31:30,780
And they were like, 10 million.

401
00:31:30,780 --> 00:31:32,780
He was talking to somebody with 10 million.

402
00:31:32,780 --> 00:31:33,780
How much will be enough?

403
00:31:33,780 --> 00:31:34,780
100 million.

404
00:31:34,780 --> 00:31:36,780
Right?

405
00:31:36,780 --> 00:31:39,780
Like even people who have more than others, they still think there's more.

406
00:31:39,780 --> 00:31:41,780
We got to get more.

407
00:31:41,780 --> 00:31:42,780
There has to be more.

408
00:31:42,780 --> 00:31:43,780
More security.

409
00:31:43,780 --> 00:31:44,780
More pleasure.

410
00:31:44,780 --> 00:31:45,780
More.

411
00:31:45,780 --> 00:31:50,780
This is the scarcity mindset.

412
00:31:50,780 --> 00:31:58,780
And Jesus says, if you want to be healthy, if you want to have abundant life, you've got to learn to trust me more than you trust yourself.

413
00:31:59,780 --> 00:32:06,780
You've got to learn to look at me as the good heavenly provider, that everything you have is from me.

414
00:32:06,780 --> 00:32:08,780
And therefore, it's not just for you.

415
00:32:08,780 --> 00:32:11,780
It is for my kingdom and your neighbor.

416
00:32:14,780 --> 00:32:15,780
Okay.

417
00:32:15,780 --> 00:32:17,780
This is why I'm excited about this series.

418
00:32:17,780 --> 00:32:20,780
Because I struggle with this.

419
00:32:20,780 --> 00:32:23,780
I feel a pull in my heart towards the scarcity mindset.

420
00:32:23,780 --> 00:32:26,780
But I believe that the invitation to Jesus is better.

421
00:32:26,780 --> 00:32:33,780
That if we can embody the abundance mindset, we will live with open hands and generous hearts.

422
00:32:33,780 --> 00:32:35,780
And we will have an abundant life.

423
00:32:36,780 --> 00:32:44,780
I'd love for you to think about, think about the person that you know that is the most generous person that you can think of right now.

424
00:32:44,780 --> 00:32:48,780
Like just take 10 seconds and hopefully, it probably won't take that long to bring to mind.

425
00:32:48,780 --> 00:32:51,780
You probably have their face in your head right now.

426
00:32:51,780 --> 00:32:53,780
Okay, look at their face in your mind.

427
00:32:53,780 --> 00:32:55,780
Are they smiling?

428
00:32:57,780 --> 00:33:00,780
Generous people are happy people.

429
00:33:00,780 --> 00:33:04,780
There's a joy that comes from living generously.

430
00:33:04,780 --> 00:33:07,780
And this is the life Jesus is inviting you to.

431
00:33:07,780 --> 00:33:11,780
And I know what you might be thinking right now because it's what I'm thinking when I'm struggling with the scarcity mindset.

432
00:33:11,780 --> 00:33:14,780
Yeah, but that person that's generous has way more than I have.

433
00:33:14,780 --> 00:33:17,780
Right?

434
00:33:17,780 --> 00:33:19,780
Generosity is not on a scale.

435
00:33:19,780 --> 00:33:21,780
It's not you can be more generous because you have more.

436
00:33:21,780 --> 00:33:22,780
It's all of us.

437
00:33:22,780 --> 00:33:25,780
What can we be generous with what we have?

438
00:33:25,780 --> 00:33:31,780
There are people that have a ton and give a ton.

439
00:33:31,780 --> 00:33:37,780
But the percentage of what they give compared to somebody that has hardly anything and yet continues to give.

440
00:33:37,780 --> 00:33:40,780
And we might look at the person that has more and say, oh, they're really generous.

441
00:33:40,780 --> 00:33:47,780
But they know when they lay their head down in bed at night that they're actually not giving much sacrificially at all.

442
00:33:47,780 --> 00:33:49,780
It's like easy for them to give that much.

443
00:33:49,780 --> 00:33:50,780
Right?

444
00:33:50,780 --> 00:33:56,780
And so we shouldn't be looking at people and rating a scale of how generous they are based on how much they give.

445
00:33:56,780 --> 00:33:59,780
It's about this mindset, scarcity, abundance.

446
00:33:59,780 --> 00:34:02,780
How do we view God and neighbor?

447
00:34:02,780 --> 00:34:05,780
It affects whether we have a good eye or a bad eye.

448
00:34:05,780 --> 00:34:07,780
Does that make sense?

449
00:34:07,780 --> 00:34:08,780
Whew.

450
00:34:08,780 --> 00:34:11,780
That's good because I got lost there for a second.

451
00:34:11,780 --> 00:34:22,780
This leads us to Christ's final teaching for the day that will help us to consider whether we are truly relying on God for our sense of security and happiness or if we have allowed money to take that place in our life.

452
00:34:22,780 --> 00:34:27,780
Kelly, if you want to come up, I'm going to try and wrap up quickly because we are running late.

453
00:34:27,780 --> 00:34:28,780
All right.

454
00:34:28,780 --> 00:34:31,780
Matthew 6, 24.

455
00:34:31,780 --> 00:34:39,780
No one can serve two masters for either he will hate the one and love the other or he will be devoted to the one and despise the other.

456
00:34:39,780 --> 00:34:43,780
You cannot serve God and money.

457
00:34:43,780 --> 00:34:55,780
So Jesus goes on here and he says that even if you like to think your life embodies the abundance mindset, if you're like, yep, I got it.

458
00:34:55,780 --> 00:34:56,780
Everything's from God.

459
00:34:56,780 --> 00:34:58,780
He's the earth, the heavenly provider.

460
00:34:58,780 --> 00:35:00,780
Everything I have comes from him.

461
00:35:00,780 --> 00:35:01,780
I'm good at that.

462
00:35:01,780 --> 00:35:02,780
I got that.

463
00:35:02,780 --> 00:35:12,780
Jesus says, are you believing that in your mind, but then hedging your bets with your stuff?

464
00:35:13,780 --> 00:35:22,780
Even if you think you'd like to think your life reflects the abundance mindset, Jesus says that we often try and have it both ways.

465
00:35:22,780 --> 00:35:38,780
We often try and intellectually and emotionally live under the abundance mindset, but then when budget season comes, when the bonus check hits, when the tax refund hits, it's like, yeah, everything comes from God, but man, this is awesome.

466
00:35:38,780 --> 00:35:39,780
I got more stuff.

467
00:35:39,780 --> 00:35:48,780
Some of your translations here say that you cannot serve God and mammon.

468
00:35:48,780 --> 00:35:50,780
Who has that in their translation?

469
00:35:50,780 --> 00:35:51,780
Anybody?

470
00:35:51,780 --> 00:35:52,780
One?

471
00:35:52,780 --> 00:35:53,780
Yeah.

472
00:35:53,780 --> 00:35:55,780
It's mostly not there anymore.

473
00:35:55,780 --> 00:36:05,780
But the reason that some translations leave it in there is because Jesus often spoke, probably spoke mostly in Aramaic, but the Gospels were written in Greek.

474
00:36:05,780 --> 00:36:14,780
And when Matthew wrote the gospel of Matthew, he wrote all of the words in Greek, except for the word for money he left in Aramaic.

475
00:36:14,780 --> 00:36:26,780
And there's a couple of different theories about why he would have done that, but whatever theory you embrace, as Bible students, we know that Matthew did that on purpose.

476
00:36:26,780 --> 00:36:29,780
So he's trying to draw our attention to something, right?

477
00:36:29,780 --> 00:36:41,780
And so my favorite theory that I think is probably most helpful, and if you're in a small group that listens to the practicing the way message, John Mark uses the other theory, which is fine.

478
00:36:41,780 --> 00:36:46,780
And it all ends up kind of coming out to the same thing.

479
00:36:46,780 --> 00:36:53,780
But most scholars think that the word mammon is actually the noun form of amen.

480
00:36:53,780 --> 00:36:57,780
Amen is trustworthy and true.

481
00:36:57,780 --> 00:37:00,780
So what is a noun of trustworthy and true?

482
00:37:00,780 --> 00:37:01,780
It's the thing you put your trust in.

483
00:37:01,780 --> 00:37:11,780
And so Jesus is saying, you cannot put your trust in God and put your trust in financial stability.

484
00:37:11,780 --> 00:37:13,780
You can't do both.

485
00:37:13,780 --> 00:37:21,780
We think we can, but we can't, because we'll either end up loving the one and hating the other, or loving the one and hating the other.

486
00:37:21,780 --> 00:37:22,780
We can't have it both ways.

487
00:37:22,780 --> 00:37:23,780
We can't hedge our bets with our stuff.

488
00:37:23,780 --> 00:37:36,780
My hunch is that many of us in the room, myself included, would like to think that we serve God as the master of our lives.

489
00:37:36,780 --> 00:37:42,780
But the way that we view and spend our money might reveal that we're trying to serve two masters at the same time.

490
00:37:42,780 --> 00:37:48,780
When we think about our money, does it lead us to feelings of fear or greed?

491
00:37:48,780 --> 00:37:54,780
If so, it's possible that we have an unhealthy relationship with our stuff.

492
00:37:54,780 --> 00:38:00,780
And I'm going to let you all sit with that for a while, because I've been sitting with it for a week and a half.

493
00:38:00,780 --> 00:38:04,780
And I very much so am struggling with this.

494
00:38:04,780 --> 00:38:07,780
It's been very revealing to my heart.

495
00:38:07,780 --> 00:38:09,780
No guilt, no condemnation.

496
00:38:09,780 --> 00:38:11,780
It's Jesus inviting me into a better life.

497
00:38:11,780 --> 00:38:16,780
This is Jesus inviting you into a better life.

498
00:38:16,780 --> 00:38:22,780
A radical, upside-down kingdom that trusts God to provide and leads to peace and generosity.

499
00:38:22,780 --> 00:38:30,780
It doesn't make sense to our earthly eyes, but when we put it in the perspective of eternity, it's the only way to live.

500
00:38:30,780 --> 00:38:36,780
So, covered a lot, big ideas.

501
00:38:36,780 --> 00:38:40,780
And ultimately, these ideas are going to apply to all of us differently.

502
00:38:40,780 --> 00:38:51,780
There are some of you in the room this morning that literally do not have enough money to provide for the absolute basic needs of you and your family.

503
00:38:51,780 --> 00:39:03,780
These principles are going to apply to you differently than they apply to the dinkers with two to six income salaries, right?

504
00:39:03,780 --> 00:39:04,780
It's just the reality.

505
00:39:04,780 --> 00:39:07,780
How these principles apply to our lives are going to apply differently.

506
00:39:07,780 --> 00:39:12,780
And so, I'm not going to try and tell you exactly how you should take these principles and apply them.

507
00:39:12,780 --> 00:39:26,780
For those of you that aren't even being able to pay your bills, the application for you might be to receive generosity from others without feeling shame or guilt.

508
00:39:26,780 --> 00:39:30,780
Knowing that it's God through them that is providing for you.

509
00:39:30,780 --> 00:39:37,780
So, how these principles apply, they apply drastically differently to all of us depending on our situation.

510
00:39:37,780 --> 00:39:42,780
My goal is not to tell you exactly how to apply these principles to your life specifically.

511
00:39:42,780 --> 00:39:53,780
Rather, I would love for you to take this principle to the Holy Spirit in prayer and ask Him what ways He might be inviting you to submit your finances to Him as the Lord and Master of your life.

512
00:39:53,780 --> 00:40:00,780
That being said, this series is called Practicing the Way.

513
00:40:00,780 --> 00:40:07,780
So, it would be foolish of me not to give you something, something that you could do, something that you could practice.

514
00:40:07,780 --> 00:40:12,780
So, here's one practice that I'd love to invite each of you to consider doing this week.

515
00:40:12,780 --> 00:40:19,780
One act of spontaneous generosity outside of your normal routine.

516
00:40:19,780 --> 00:40:21,780
Set aside a specific amount.

517
00:40:21,780 --> 00:40:22,780
It can be a little.

518
00:40:22,780 --> 00:40:23,780
It can be a lot.

519
00:40:23,780 --> 00:40:24,780
It can be a lot.

520
00:40:24,780 --> 00:40:32,780
If you don't have any margin in your budget at all, maybe you have a possession that is valuable to you that you know would bless somebody else.

521
00:40:32,780 --> 00:40:38,780
Maybe that's how you express to God that you trust Him as the abundant good creator.

522
00:40:38,780 --> 00:40:40,780
I don't know what it looks like for you.

523
00:40:40,780 --> 00:40:42,780
But set aside a specific amount.

524
00:40:42,780 --> 00:40:43,780
Take cash out of an ATM.

525
00:40:43,780 --> 00:40:46,780
Earmark it in your budget.

526
00:40:46,780 --> 00:40:48,780
And take it to God in prayer.

527
00:40:48,780 --> 00:40:53,780
Ask God to give you the opportunity to bless someone.

528
00:40:53,780 --> 00:40:54,780
And then keep your eyes open.

529
00:40:54,780 --> 00:41:03,780
Look around your circles of influence for someone that might be blessed by your act of generosity.

530
00:41:03,780 --> 00:41:06,780
Buy someone behind you in line a coffee.

531
00:41:06,780 --> 00:41:08,780
Anonymously pay for a family's lunch.

532
00:41:08,780 --> 00:41:14,780
Drop off groceries or a gift to someone you know that is in need or has experienced suffering.

533
00:41:14,780 --> 00:41:19,780
Send cash digitally to help a friend with medical bills or an expense that they can't afford to pay.

534
00:41:19,780 --> 00:41:22,780
Buy a gift.

535
00:41:22,780 --> 00:41:23,780
Send it to someone.

536
00:41:23,780 --> 00:41:24,780
Encourage them.

537
00:41:24,780 --> 00:41:25,780
Bless them.

538
00:41:25,780 --> 00:41:26,780
Give a possession away.

539
00:41:26,780 --> 00:41:29,780
Whatever it might be.

540
00:41:29,780 --> 00:41:35,780
Make one act of spontaneous generosity.

541
00:41:35,780 --> 00:41:42,780
And then think about how you felt when you did that act of generosity.

542
00:41:43,780 --> 00:41:50,780
I would love to tell you that the moment you do the act of generosity, you're going to feel a deep sense of joy and happiness.

543
00:41:50,780 --> 00:41:56,780
But I like, I worked on this this week.

544
00:41:56,780 --> 00:42:02,780
And as I was giving the gift, I was like, oh, I kind of would really like to keep this.

545
00:42:02,780 --> 00:42:09,780
Right?

546
00:42:09,780 --> 00:42:12,780
What does that tell me about my heart?

547
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:16,780
What does that reveal to me about my relationship with God and money?

548
00:42:16,780 --> 00:42:18,780
It's a helpful revelation.

549
00:42:18,780 --> 00:42:30,780
And as I continue this practice week after week, my hope and my prayer is that I continue to come back to the Lord in prayer and say, God, I want to have an abundance mindset, but I often have a scarcity mindset.

550
00:42:30,780 --> 00:42:34,780
So yet again, I am going to give away and see how it makes me feel.

551
00:42:34,780 --> 00:42:41,780
And my hope and my hope and my prayer is that for those of us that are struggling with a scarcity mindset, it's not going to be an immediate.

552
00:42:41,780 --> 00:42:42,780
For some of us, it might be.

553
00:42:42,780 --> 00:42:46,780
You might give the one thing away and you're like, this is the greatest feeling I've ever had in my life.

554
00:42:47,780 --> 00:42:51,780
And for some of you, you might be like me and be like, oh, I kind of liked that thing.

555
00:42:51,780 --> 00:42:54,780
I wanted to keep it, but I'm doing the thing Jesus told me to do.

556
00:42:54,780 --> 00:42:55,780
Yay.

557
00:42:55,780 --> 00:43:09,880
But as we put these things into practice, as we take Jesus at his word, I have followed Jesus long enough to know that doing what he says leads to abundant life.

558
00:43:10,780 --> 00:43:19,620
And that not doing what he says feels good at times, but always falls short of what I wanted to accomplish in my life.

559
00:43:19,620 --> 00:43:26,660
Jesus says, blessed are those who hear what I have to say and do what I have to say.

560
00:43:26,660 --> 00:43:31,640
So I encourage you to pray about how you can put this teaching into action this week.

561
00:43:31,640 --> 00:43:34,540
Consider it how it made you feel.

562
00:43:34,540 --> 00:43:37,980
Get with somebody that loves Jesus that you trust and talk about it.

563
00:43:37,980 --> 00:43:40,180
Talk about how that thing made you feel.

564
00:43:40,180 --> 00:43:41,540
Many of you are going to be in small groups.

565
00:43:41,540 --> 00:43:44,480
You're going to do this together and talk about how did it make you feel?

566
00:43:44,480 --> 00:43:45,840
Why did it make you feel that way?

567
00:43:45,840 --> 00:43:48,220
What might that reveal about your heart?

568
00:43:48,220 --> 00:43:49,400
Sound good?

569
00:43:49,400 --> 00:43:51,580
Let's pray.

570
00:43:51,580 --> 00:43:56,320
Father in heaven, you are so, so good.

571
00:43:56,320 --> 00:44:03,820
You are a loving father who has created out of your generous nature.

572
00:44:03,820 --> 00:44:08,100
You have given us good gifts.

573
00:44:09,700 --> 00:44:11,000
Think about the Garden of Eden.

574
00:44:11,000 --> 00:44:16,580
And throughout the creation account, it says, God gave, God gave, God gave.

575
00:44:16,580 --> 00:44:20,200
And then it says, Adam and Eve took.

576
00:44:23,140 --> 00:44:28,600
We are where we are today as a society because you have freely given and we have taken and run.

577
00:44:28,600 --> 00:44:40,420
God, may we learn as people who profess faith in Jesus to stop taking and to start giving.

578
00:44:43,300 --> 00:44:44,600
For your glory for your glory for our good.

579
00:44:44,600 --> 00:44:45,440
For your glory for our good.

580
00:44:45,440 --> 00:44:47,320
In Jesus' name I pray.

581
00:44:47,320 --> 00:44:47,980
Amen.

582
00:44:49,980 --> 00:44:58,080
Really quick, practical thing that I want to do in light of a message on generosity that was somewhat heavy hitting and hard.

583
00:44:59,280 --> 00:45:05,000
I want to give you thanks for the generosity that you all have expressed.

584
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:10,160
You probably drove on a new paved and painted parking lot this morning.

585
00:45:10,160 --> 00:45:11,480
Yeah?

586
00:45:11,480 --> 00:45:12,940
Did it feel good on the struts?

587
00:45:12,940 --> 00:45:13,380
Yeah?

588
00:45:15,960 --> 00:45:17,160
I want to do a couple of things.

